Refutation complete. Verdict appended to `AUREL_RESEARCH/findings/2026-11-05.md` under a `[REFUTE]` header dated 14:25.

**Target.** Two research-lane entries landed since the 11:25 run. cycle4 concluded null, so there was nothing to break there. cycle3 carried the newest weak signal: the paper ledger's 305 closed re-accel trades average +0.176R, the sign is "already stable" (n* of 200, P(sum>0) near 0.99), the first and second halves agree, and the figure is five times the recent scan. No promotion candidate exists, so this was the only material.

**Verdict: inconclusive by the pre-registered rule, and it splits three ways.**

| Claim | Test | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Sign already stable | Only trades entered after the last recipe change on 10-24, 70 trades | mean +0.146, t 0.71, P(sum>0) 0.75. Broken for the forward-only part. |
| Same, pooled 305 with day-block bootstrap | n* rises from 200 to 300; P at n=305 is 0.97. Top three days supply 62% of the total. | Survives weakly. |
| Five times the scan | Day-block resampling of 305 trades from three recent-window scan nulls | P(mean ≥ +0.176) is 0.006, 0.005, 0.026. Two of three pass Bonferroni. The gap is real. |
| Same, forward-only 70 trades | p 0.15 | Indistinguishable from the scan null. |
| In/out consistent | Split at the last recipe change instead of the time median | Out-of-sample inside a ±0.25R interval that admits almost anything. The forward set's own halves go +0.37 then −0.07. |

**What the ledger actually is.** It is not a single pre-registered recipe run forward. Sixty-seven trades predate the re-accel code itself. The variant was designed on 09-29 from three trades of 09-28 and then backfilled to 09-15. The minimum stop width was fixed on 09-30 after re-simulating the same period, by the engine's own comment. The booking rule tightened on 10-24, and closed trades are frozen, so 235 trades carry the lenient booking and 70 the strict one. I confirmed this against the chart server's bars: 103 of 103 pre-10-24 trades reproduce under the old rule and 64 of 64 post-10-24 trades under the new one. Rebooking everything strictly would move the mean to roughly +0.144. No closed trade's R was ever rewritten, so the ledger is honest, just mixed.

**Most serious counter-evidence recorded.** Seventy trades have little power. With a true mean of +0.15 the chance of reaching t 2 is about one in five, so "cannot show stability" is not "no edge." Excluding only the backfill leaves 238 trades at t 1.94, close to cycle3's claim. Revival condition: forward trades from 10-24 onward reaching 200 with day-cluster t at or above 2 and p below 0.05 against the 2026 scan null, about five more weeks at the current pace.

**Lessons written for the research lane.** Stratify any ledger figure by the engine's git history before counting "forward n". Cut in/out at the last recipe change, not the time median. Test "is the ledger chance from the scan" as P(mean ≥ observed), not P(sum>0), which changes the answer here from 0.6 to 0.006. Use day blocks for the sign-stability bootstrap.

